RBI/2017-18/40, para 6, the Board of Directors of an SFB must consider the following four factors when evaluating a proposal for declaration of dividend:

1. The divergence in asset classification and provisioning for Non-Performing Assets (NPAs), including its trend, as observed under supervisory findings of the Reserve Bank (RBI/2017-18/40, para 6(1));
2. The auditors' report to the financial statements, including modified opinion or emphasis of matter, for the financial year in which the dividend is proposed (RBI/2017-18/40, para 6(2));
3. The current and projected capital position vis-à-vis applicable regulatory capital requirements (RBI/2017-18/40, para 6(3)); and
4. The long-term growth plans of the bank (RBI/2017-18/40, para 6(4)).

These factors are essential for banks to ensure compliance with regulatory requirements and maintain sound financial practices.

